      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1791363994805,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "A memory space is the computer's memory seen\nas one long numbered list of slots. \nEach slot holds one byte and has a number, called its address.\nA program's data and instructions live in those slots.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "A memory space is the computer's memory seen\nas one long numbered list of slots. \nEach slot holds one byte and has a number, called its address.\nA program's data and instructions live in those slots.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "ugHwfBEMCL89h6VTTOKM5",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 436,
